<Ui>
    <!--
        The GAME MENU — the frame ESC opens (decision 0674). The last hole in the game shell's
        outermost layer: until now ESC's chain ran out of things to close and did nothing, and the
        Main Menu micro button was drawn but dead (MicroMenu.xml's SCOPE note).

        PROVENANCE (0985 — the three-source split, stated the same way in every era-shaped
        window; OptionsFrame.xml carries the sibling block):
        · STRUCTURE & BEHAVIOR — the 1.15 era client (wow-ui-source-era @ 1.15.9.68940): the
          ladder shape, its groups and gaps, which entries exist (the SCOPE section below).
          If 1.15 has the mechanism, it STAYS.
        · CHROME MECHANISM — this window predates 1.13: the 1.12 client's OWN GameMenuFrame
          is the chrome ground truth (the dialog backdrop, header plate, red buttons — the
          same dialog family the 1.13/1.14 options windows kept), quoted below.
        · ART BYTES — the 1.12 MPQ chain only; nothing later-client at runtime (0978's law).

        Ground truth, all quoted rather than re-derived:
        · **The frame** — ref `GameMenuFrame.xml` (patch.MPQ, extracted): 195x246, `frameStrata`
          DIALOG, the UI-DialogBox backdrop with the 11/12/12/11 insets and 32px tile/edge, the
          256x64 UI-DialogBox-Header at TOP +12 with MAIN_MENU centered 14px down it, and the
          eight-button ladder — first button CENTER on the frame's TOP at (0,-37), each next one
          TOP-to-BOTTOM at (0,-1), and Return to Game hung (0,-16) below Exit Game (the one gap in
          the stack, which is what makes the last entry read as separate).
        · **The button** — ref `GameMenuButtonTemplate` (UIPanelTemplates.xml l.403-410): a 144x21
          `UIPanelButtonTemplate` (the UI-Panel-Button Up/Down/Disabled/Highlight four-state art,
          TexCoords 0..0.625 / 0..0.6875) whose label trio is overridden to
          GameFontHighlight/GameFontHighlight/GameFontDisable — i.e. the menu's labels are WHITE,
          not the gold a normal panel button wears, and grey when disabled.
        · **The labels** — GlobalStrings.lua (patch-2.MPQ), verbatim: VIDEOOPTIONS_MENU "Video
          Options", SOUNDOPTIONS_MENU "Sound Options", UIOPTIONS_MENU "Interface Options",
          MACROS "Macros", LOGOUT "Logout", EXIT_GAME "Exit Game",
          RETURN_TO_GAME "Return to Game", MAIN_MENU "Main Menu". Declared as the real globals
          (they are addon-visible API, decision 0068) and read back into each button's label in its
          OnLoad — the ref's `text="LOGOUT"` attribute IS a global lookup, which this engine's
          literal `text=` is not.
        · **The sounds** — the ref's own OnClick lines: igMainMenuOption (the five option buttons),
          igMainMenuLogout, igMainMenuQuit, igMainMenuContinue. All four kits verified present in
          SoundEntries.dbc (patch-2.MPQ) alongside the igMainMenuOpen/Close pair already in use.
        · **The two logout dialogs** — ref `StaticPopup.lua` l.564-600 (CAMP + QUIT) is the
          SPECIFICATION for them: the two dialog keys, the field names, the 20 s timeout and the
          asymmetric button sets are contract, and the entries carrying them are written here in
          our own shape on the shared popup engine (UiPanels.xml), whose countdown-text branch
          already lists both `which` names. Their driver events are the reference's own
          (`re/events/event-catalog.tsv`: 276 PLAYER_CAMPING, 277 PLAYER_QUITING,
          278 LOGOUT_CANCEL), fired by `crate::ui_logout` off `SMSG_LOGOUT_RESPONSE`.

        NAMES are the reference's, unprefixed (`GameMenuFrame`, `GameMenuButton*`) — the same call
        MicroMenu.xml made for its straight transcriptions, and required here besides: `ToggleGameMenu`
        and `GameMenuFrame` are Era API surface an addon addresses by name.

        SCOPE / divergences (noted, not bugs):
        - **The ladder is the ERA menu's** (director's call on the 0951 review — supersedes 0951
          §3's five-button collapse): the Era client's own ESC menu shape, greyed where benilla
          has nothing behind the entry yet. Geometry quoted from the era dump @ 1.15.9 (Gethe
          wow-ui-source, classic_era, the 0950 pin):
          · Blizzard_SharedXML/Classic/Frame/MainMenuFrameTemplates.xml l.18-33 — the menu is a
            VerticalLayoutFrame, buttonTemplate MainMenuFrameButtonTemplate, padding
            top/bottom/left/right = 32/28/28/28, spacing 0; l.11-16 — the button is a 144x21
            UIPanelButtonTemplate with the white/white/grey label trio (the SAME art + trio the
            1.12 GameMenuButtonTemplate carries — no era-only art in this menu at all).
          · Shared/Frame/MainMenuFrameTemplates.lua l.61-71 — AddSection() puts a 20-unit gap
            (the next button's topPadding) between groups; AddCloseButton uses the same 20.
          · Shared/GameMenuFrame.lua l.62-162 — the Era ladder: Options · [gap] · AddOns, Edit
            Mode, Support, Macros · [gap] · Logout, Exit Game · [gap] · Return to Game. (Store /
            Rewards / What's New / Ratings are structurally off in Era — store disabled, no
            account store, IsStandard() false, koKR only.)
          · The layout math those constants produce, precomputed here (this engine has no layout
            frames) — for OUR seven rungs, the era's eight minus AddOns (next bullet): width
            28+144+28 = 200; button tops 32/73/94/115/156/177/218; height 218+21+28 = 267.
            Anchored as a TOPLEFT chain so the gaps read in the XML.
          · No Key Bindings rung — the era menu's own shape: 1.15 ceded the entry to the
            Settings panel, and since decision 1008 ours lives there too (the Options window's
            Keybindings category, KeyBindingsPage.xml). 0997 had carved the 1.13/1.14 seat back
            in for its standalone window; that seat left with the window.
          · No AddOns rung — the director's call: the char-select AddOns screen
            (`char_select::addons`, the reference's own glue-side home for this list) is the only
            addon UI. The in-game panel 1197 put behind this rung (AddonList.xml) is retired,
            and the rung left with it — 1.12's own ESC menu has no AddOns row either.
          · The header — Classic/Dialog/DialogTemplates.xml l.11-43 (ClassicDialogHeaderTemplate):
            the same 256x64 UI-DialogBox-Header art, text = MAINMENU_BUTTON, swapped to
            GameFontNormalMed1 (13px) by MainMenuFrameMixin:OnLoad. Both header idioms (1.12's
            TOP+12 texture / era's 39-tall frame with the art centered) seat the art within half
            a unit of each other; the 1.12 transcription is kept, the font and string are era's.
        - **Edit Mode / Support ship DISABLED** — nothing behind them yet
          (`GameMenuButton_Pending`): the template's own `-Disabled` art + grey label, exactly
          how the era menu greys a dead entry (SetEnabled(false) → DisabledFont). Each goes live
          by deleting one `GameMenuButton_Pending` call and writing its OnClick.
        - The Options label stays a literal "Options": 1.12 GlobalStrings has no era
          GAMEMENU_OPTIONS (checked; its OPTIONS_MENU is "Options Menu", a different string).
        - The ref frame is `toplevel="true" movable="true" parent="UIParent"`. Dropped: this engine has
          no cross-file `parent=` attachment (SkillFrame.xml's header comment), and `movable` is inert
          in the ref too (GameMenuFrame defines no drag scripts, so it never actually moves).
          `frameStrata="DIALOG"` is what puts it over the world UI, and that is kept.
          **The "no frame-level raise" half of that reason is gone**: the raise law is built
          (`script::object::toplevel`, wow-re `ui/scratch/toplevel-raise.md`) and the loader honours
          `toplevel="true"`. Re-adding it here is a one-word change and would make the Esc menu come
          to the front over any other DIALOG-strata frame it overlaps; left off pending the
          director's call on the look, not on the mechanism.
    -->
    <Script><![CDATA[
        -- The reference GlobalStrings (patch-2.MPQ Interface\FrameXML\GlobalStrings.lua), quoted
        -- verbatim. `X = X or "..."` so a later real strings table wins, the MicroMenu.xml idiom.
        MAIN_MENU = MAIN_MENU or "Main Menu"
        HUD_EDIT_MODE_MENU = HUD_EDIT_MODE_MENU or "Edit Mode"
        GAMEMENU_SUPPORT = GAMEMENU_SUPPORT or "Support"
        MACROS = MACROS or "Macros"
        LOGOUT = LOGOUT or "Logout"
        EXIT_GAME = EXIT_GAME or "Exit Game"
        RETURN_TO_GAME = RETURN_TO_GAME or "Return to Game"
        CAMP_TIMER = CAMP_TIMER or "%d %s until logout"
        QUIT_TIMER = QUIT_TIMER or "%d %s until exit"
        QUIT_NOW = QUIT_NOW or "Exit now"
        CANCEL = CANCEL or "Cancel"

        -- One label setter for a button with nothing behind it yet (Edit Mode and Support): set
        -- the ref's text, then disable (grey label + the template's -Disabled art). Making it
        -- live is deleting the call and writing its ref OnClick.
        function GameMenuButton_Pending(button, text)
            button:SetText(text)
            button:Disable()
        end

        -- ── The two logout dialogs (spec: StaticPopup.lua l.564-600) ────────────────────────────
        -- Both are countdown dialogs: their `text` is a format string the popup engine's per-tick
        -- branch fills with the remaining time (StaticPopup_OnUpdate's which-list already names CAMP
        -- and QUIT), so they open blank and count down. `timeout = 20` matches the server's own
        -- logout timer (vmangos `WorldSession::LogoutRequest` → 20 s), which is what the countdown
        -- is displaying — the client is not the authority here, it is narrating the server's clock.
        --
        -- The asymmetry between them is the spec's: CAMP offers only Cancel (the commented-out
        -- CAMP_NOW/ForceLogout button is dead in 1.12 — "uncomment once forced logouts are completely
        -- implemented"), while QUIT offers Exit now + Cancel, because a force-quit needs no server
        -- round trip.
        --
        -- Both entries below are written scalars-first, handlers-last, so the dialog's SHAPE reads
        -- before its behaviour does.

        -- Dismissing a running countdown means "I didn't mean it": call the logout off. Only while
        -- it is still RUNNING, though — the popup engine zeroes `timeleft` before hiding a dialog
        -- that expired, so reaching zero leaves the logout alone. (Backwards, and every logout in
        -- the field is cancelled by its own dialog at t=0 and the character never leaves.) One
        -- function because both dialogs mean exactly this; `this` is the popup frame, which the
        -- engine has bound around the handler.
        local function CancelLogoutIfStillCounting()
            if this.timeleft > 0 then
                CancelLogout()
            end
        end

        StaticPopupDialogs["CAMP"] = {
            text = CAMP_TIMER,
            button1 = CANCEL,
            timeout = 20,
            whileDead = 1,
            hideOnEscape = 1,
            OnAccept = function()
                CancelLogout()
            end,
            OnHide = CancelLogoutIfStillCounting,
        }

        StaticPopupDialogs["QUIT"] = {
            text = QUIT_TIMER,
            button1 = QUIT_NOW,
            button2 = CANCEL,
            timeout = 20,
            whileDead = 1,
            hideOnEscape = 1,
            -- A force-quit needs no server round trip, so the countdown it was narrating is over
            -- the moment the button is pressed: zero `timeleft` so the OnHide below stands down.
            OnAccept = function()
                ForceQuit()
                this.timeleft = 0
            end,
            OnHide = CancelLogoutIfStillCounting,
        }

        -- The camp/quit event driver. The ref handles these three in UIParent's own OnEvent
        -- (UIParent.lua l.304-315); benilla has no UIParent frame, so this is a dedicated hidden
        -- listener — the BenillaDeleteItemConfirmDriver shape.
        function BenillaLogoutDriver_OnEvent()
            if event == "PLAYER_CAMPING" then
                StaticPopup_Show("CAMP")
            elseif event == "PLAYER_QUITING" then
                StaticPopup_Show("QUIT")
            elseif event == "LOGOUT_CANCEL" then
                StaticPopup_Hide("CAMP")
                StaticPopup_Hide("QUIT")
            end
        end
    ]]></Script>

    <!-- The era header text size (Classic/Dialog/DialogTemplates.xml + the OnLoad font swap):
         GameFontNormalMed1 = SystemFont_Med2 = FRIZQT 13, gold, the MasterFont shadow. Era's
         name, declared here beside its one consumer (the 0951 residue convention: Fonts.xml
         stays the complete 1.12 set). -->
    <Font name="GameFontNormalMed1" inherits="GameFontNormal" virtual="true">
        <FontHeight><AbsValue val="13"/></FontHeight>
    </Font>

    <!-- `GameMenuButtonTemplate` MOVED OUT, to UIPanelTemplates.xml — the reference's own file for
         it (ref UIPanelTemplates.xml l.403-410), and now ColorPickerFrame.xml's Okay/Cancel need it
         too, from far above this file's LAST-in-the-toc seat. It lived here, with its four state
         textures inlined, only because `UIPanelButtonTemplate` had not been transcribed yet; it now
         has been, so the reference's actual body (`inherits="UIPanelButtonTemplate"`, 144x21, the
         white/white/grey label trio) replaces the private copy verbatim. Era's
         MainMenuFrameButtonTemplate (Classic/Frame/MainMenuFrameTemplates.xml l.11-16) is that same
         button — same art, same trio, same size — so the header's ART BYTES note is unchanged. -->

    <!-- `toplevel` is the ref's own (GameMenuFrame.xml l.3) and was dropped here: without the bit
         a DIALOG-strata window opened over another one stays behind it (the B180/Bagnon class,
         decision 1318). Restored alone; the ref's `movable`/`parent` stay off deliberately. -->
    <Frame name="GameMenuFrame" frameStrata="DIALOG" toplevel="true" enableMouse="true" hidden="true">
        <!-- The era layout engine's own numbers (header SCOPE note): 28+144+28 wide, 32-top /
             28-bottom padding around our seven 21-unit rungs with three 20-unit section gaps. -->
        <Size><AbsDimension x="200" y="267"/></Size>
        <Anchors><Anchor point="CENTER"/></Anchors>
        <Backdrop bgFile="Interface\DialogFrame\UI-DialogBox-Background" edgeFile="Interface\DialogFrame\UI-DialogBox-Border" tile="true">
            <BackgroundInsets><AbsInset left="11" right="12" top="12" bottom="11"/></BackgroundInsets>
            <TileSize><AbsValue val="32"/></TileSize>
            <EdgeSize><AbsValue val="32"/></EdgeSize>
        </Backdrop>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <Texture name="GameMenuFrameHeader" file="Interface\DialogFrame\UI-DialogBox-Header">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="64"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOP"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="12"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <!-- Era swaps the header text to 13px (MainMenuFrameMixin:OnLoad →
                     SetHeaderFont(GameFontNormalMed1)); the seat is the 1.12 one (within half a
                     unit of era's — header SCOPE note). -->
                <FontString name="GameMenuFrameTitle" inherits="GameFontNormalMed1">
                    <Anchors>
                        <Anchor point="TOP" relativeTo="GameMenuFrameHeader"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-14"/></Offset></Anchor>
                    </Anchors>
                </FontString>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <Frames>
            <!-- The era ladder minus its AddOns rung (header SCOPE notes): Options · gap ·
                 Edit Mode, Support, Macros · gap · Logout, Exit Game · gap · Return to Game.
                 A TOPLEFT chain at the era layout engine's numbers — x 28, first top -32, 0
                 between group members, -20 at each section break. Live entries wire the era
                 OnClick intent; pending ones grey out through GameMenuButton_Pending until
                 something exists behind them. -->

            <!-- Options — live: the era GameMenuFrame.lua l.88 entry (ShowUIPanel(SettingsPanel)
                 there, OptionsFrame here) plus an explicit HideUIPanel first. The ref leans on
                 the center-replacement rule for the swap (ShowUIPanel l.697-702: native-center
                 frames replace each other); hiding the menu explicitly says the same thing
                 without relying on the eviction path. -->
            <Button name="GameMenuButtonOptions" inherits="GameMenuButtonTemplate">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="28" y="-32"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Scripts>
                    <OnLoad>self:SetText("Options")</OnLoad>
                    <OnClick>
                        PlaySound("igMainMenuOption")
                        HideUIPanel(GameMenuFrame)
                        ShowUIPanel(OptionsFrame)
                    </OnClick>
                </Scripts>
            </Button>

            <Button name="GameMenuButtonEditMode" inherits="GameMenuButtonTemplate">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GameMenuButtonOptions" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-20"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Scripts><OnLoad>GameMenuButton_Pending(self, HUD_EDIT_MODE_MENU)</OnLoad></Scripts>
            </Button>
            <Button name="GameMenuButtonSupport" inherits="GameMenuButtonTemplate">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GameMenuButtonEditMode" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Scripts><OnLoad>GameMenuButton_Pending(self, GAMEMENU_SUPPORT)</OnLoad></Scripts>
            </Button>
            <Button name="GameMenuButtonMacros" inherits="GameMenuButtonTemplate">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GameMenuButtonSupport" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <!-- LIVE since decision 0983 (MacroFrame.xml). The ref's own body
                     (GameMenuFrame.xml l.118-122): hide the menu, then ShowMacroFrame(). -->
                <Scripts>
                    <OnLoad>self:SetText(MACROS)</OnLoad>
                    <OnClick>
                        PlaySound("igMainMenuOption")
                        HideUIPanel(getglobal("GameMenuFrame"))
                        ShowMacroFrame()
                    </OnClick>
                </Scripts>
            </Button>

            <!-- The three that are live. The ref's OnShow on both Logout and Quit disables the
                 button while either logout dialog is already up (you cannot re-arm a running
                 countdown); it runs on the menu's own show, which is when a re-opened menu has to
                 re-read that state. -->
            <Button name="GameMenuButtonLogout" inherits="GameMenuButtonTemplate">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GameMenuButtonMacros" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-20"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Scripts>
                    <OnLoad>self:SetText(LOGOUT)</OnLoad>
                    <OnShow>
                        if not StaticPopup_Visible("CAMP") and not StaticPopup_Visible("QUIT") then
                            self:Enable()
                        else
                            self:Disable()
                        end
                    </OnShow>
                    <OnClick>
                        PlaySound("igMainMenuLogout")
                        Logout()
                        HideUIPanel(GameMenuFrame)
                    </OnClick>
                </Scripts>
            </Button>
            <Button name="GameMenuButtonQuit" inherits="GameMenuButtonTemplate">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GameMenuButtonLogout" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Scripts>
                    <OnLoad>self:SetText(EXIT_GAME)</OnLoad>
                    <OnShow>
                        if not StaticPopup_Visible("CAMP") and not StaticPopup_Visible("QUIT") then
                            self:Enable()
                        else
                            self:Disable()
                        end
                    </OnShow>
                    <OnClick>
                        PlaySound("igMainMenuQuit")
                        Quit()
                        HideUIPanel(GameMenuFrame)
                    </OnClick>
                </Scripts>
            </Button>
            <Button name="GameMenuButtonContinue" inherits="GameMenuButtonTemplate">
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="GameMenuButtonQuit" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-20"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Scripts>
                    <OnLoad>self:SetText(RETURN_TO_GAME)</OnLoad>
                    <OnClick>
                        PlaySound("igMainMenuContinue")
                        HideUIPanel(GameMenuFrame)
                    </OnClick>
                </Scripts>
            </Button>
        </Frames>
        <!-- ref GameMenuFrame OnShow/OnHide, verbatim: the micro row's Main Menu button pushes in
             while the menu is up, and the bag bar greys out under it (you cannot open bags from
             behind the menu — ShowUIPanel's center gate would refuse the window anyway, so the
             greying is the visible half of a rule the panel manager already enforces). Guarded, the
             UiPanels.xml `CloseMenus and CloseMenus()` posture: a headless test loads this file
             without the action bar behind it. -->
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>GameMenuFrameTitle:SetText(MAIN_MENU)</OnLoad>
            <OnShow>
                -- The shared era-window scale first (ERA_WINDOW_SCALE, OptionsFrame.xml — loaded
                -- before this file): the era menu has no scale of its own (GameMenuFrame.xml +
                -- MainMenuFrameTemplates, grepped clean), it draws at UIParent's px-per-unit —
                -- the SAME density as the era options window, whose checkFit caps at 1. The knob
                -- is our stand-in for that UIParent scale; without it the menu drew 28% larger
                -- relative to the options window than the era pair ("esc menu scale too big" —
                -- director, 2026-08-04). `or 1` guards a load-order regression only. NOTE: this
                -- lives INSIDE the existing OnShow — a second Scripts/OnShow block on the same
                -- frame would silently REPLACE this one (SetScript semantics: last wins).
                this:SetScale(ERA_WINDOW_SCALE or 1)
                if UpdateMicroButtons then UpdateMicroButtons() end
                if Disable_BagButtons then Disable_BagButtons() end
            </OnShow>
            <OnHide>
                if UpdateMicroButtons then UpdateMicroButtons() end
                if Enable_BagButtons then Enable_BagButtons() end
            </OnHide>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>

    <!-- The camp/quit event listener (the ref's UIParent OnEvent arms — script block above). -->
    <Frame name="BenillaLogoutDriver" hidden="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="1" y="1"/></Size>
        <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"/></Anchors>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>
                self:RegisterEvent("PLAYER_CAMPING")
                self:RegisterEvent("PLAYER_QUITING")
                self:RegisterEvent("LOGOUT_CANCEL")
            </OnLoad>
            <OnEvent>BenillaLogoutDriver_OnEvent()</OnEvent>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>
</Ui>
